libusb (app/src/main/cpp/include/libusb.h,
        app/src/main/cpp/libs/arm64-v8a/libusb-1.0.a)

Cross-platform USB library. Statically linked into the native engine so
the app can drive a UAC2 USB DAC via libusb_wrap_sys_device() against the
UsbDeviceConnection file descriptor granted by Android.

Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 or later.
Source: https://libusb.info/ — https://github.com/libusb/libusb

Under LGPL-2.1 §6, binaries that statically link libusb must permit the
user to relink with a modified libusb. This requirement is satisfied by
(a) this attribution notice, (b) distributing the statically-compiled
archive and header so the user can rebuild the app against their own
libusb, and (c) keeping the libusb build recipe documented in
BUILD_SUMMARY.md.

