r8brain-free-src (app/src/main/cpp/third_party/r8brain-free-src/)

High-quality sample rate converter (Aleksey Vaneev / Voxengo), used to
resample REW-exported room-correction impulse responses from their
native measurement rate to the engine's fixed 176400Hz output rate,
once at load time. Vendored header-only, configured to use its bundled
Ooura FFT4G backend (fft/fft4g.h) rather than PFFFT.

Licensed under the MIT License.
Source: https://github.com/avaneev/r8brain-free-src
Vendored from commit e71c31bf320f84210bb4bdcb57e296c39ce940f9.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
PFFFT (app/src/main/cpp/third_party/pffft/)

"Pretty Fast FFT" — single-precision, SIMD-accelerated 1-D FFT (Julien
Pommier). Used as the FFT primitive for room-correction's
FFT-partitioned overlap-save convolver. Vendored as source; the NEON
code path is active on the arm64-v8a build.

Derived from FFTPACKv4/v5 by Dr Paul Swarztrauber (NCAR); licensed
under the NCAR/UCAR FFTPACK license (a BSD-3-Clause-style permissive
license — see the header of pffft.h/pffft.c for the full text).
Source: https://bitbucket.org/jpommier/pffft
Vendored from commit 09796885cd5b9da5692242de2df0d81e5e1f3d21.

